          "code": "ASSIST_USER_IN_ENTERING_NOTES",
          "id": "1779864928509",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779864928513_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Supply Chain Planner.\n\n##INPUT:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}}\n\n##TASK:\nRewrite the user input into clear, professional supply-chain planning language while preserving the original business intent.\n\n##RULES:\n1. Include ALL information from the user input.\n2. Do NOT add information that is not explicitly stated.\n3. Expand abbreviated words when the meaning is obvious from context.\n4. Preserve product numbers, SKU numbers, dates, quantities, percentages, planner terminology, customer names, and person names exactly as provided.\n5. Convert fragmented notes into complete professional sentences.\n6. If the input contains an email, chat message, subject line, or quoted text, summarize it professionally while preserving the original meaning.\n7. If the input contains multiple statements, generate multiple HTML paragraphs.\n8. Do not invent explanations, assumptions, business reasons, or context.\n9. Do not include introductory phrases such as:\n   * \"Sure\"\n   * \"Here's the rephrased version\"\n   * \"Rewritten text\"\n10. Output ONLY valid HTML snippets using:\n\t* <p>\n\t* <strong> when emphasis improves readability\n\t* <time> when a date is explicitly provided\n11. Do not output markdown.\n12. Do not output code fences.\n13. Do not output multiple alternative responses.\n\n##ABBREVIATION HANDLING:\nExpand abbreviations only when the expansion is directly inferable from the text.\n\tExamples:\n\t* pc → pieces\n\t* po → purchase order\n\t* promo → promotion\n\t* comp → accommodate\n\t* qty → quantity\nIf the meaning is uncertain, retain the original abbreviation.\n\n##OUTPUT FORMAT:\nReturn only HTML.\n\n##EXAMPLES##\nInput:\nABC agreed to remove 550pc from P3 NR\nOutput:\n<p>ABC has agreed to remove 550 pieces from P3 NR.</p>\n\nInput:\nRemoved 250 units which was moved from October\nOutput:\n<p>A total of 250 units that had been moved from October have been removed.</p>\n\nInput:\nRemoved overrides since stat is aligned to avg POS 68/month with 9 WOS\nOutput:\n<p>The overrides have been removed because the statistical forecast is aligned with the average point of sale of 68 units per month and 9 weeks of supply.</p>\n\nInput:\n240143 Truckload event, drive accessories with a 25% discount and getting Free Goods in\nOutput:\n<p>A <strong>240143 Truckload event</strong> is offering a <strong>25% discount</strong> on <strong>drive accessories</strong>, along with <strong>free goods</strong> as an additional incentive.</p>\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"aiAssistedNotes\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
